const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/commercial/dishwasher-repair/glass-washer-repair/";

const title = "Commercial Glass Washer Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = "Commercial bar glass washer repair across Southern California. Spinning wash arms, dispensers, drain pumps. BHGS #A49573.";

const faqs = [
  { q: "Why is my bar glass washer producing hazy glassware?", a: "A bar glass washer producing hazy glassware almost always traces to chemistry calibration rather than mechanical failure on commercial bar models (CMA Glass Mizer, Jackson Avenger LT glasswasher, Champion CG-2, Lamb, Moyer Diebel, Hoshizaki HG-100). (1) Detergent dispenser pickup tube pinched, clogged, or miscalibrated — detergent dose drops below spec, soap film not fully removed during rinse cycle. $180-$320 pickup tube + pump rebuild + chemistry calibration. (2) Rinse-aid dispenser miscalibrated — rinse aid dose drops below spec, water doesn't sheet off glassware cleanly, leaves spots. $180-$320 rebuild + calibration. (3) Sanitizer pickup tube wear or calibration drift — sanitizer concentration drops below spec (typically 50-100 ppm chlorine for low-temp chemical sanitizing). $180-$320 + calibration. Plus LADWP hard water contribution (high mineral content amplifies hazy glassware issues if rinse-aid not perfectly calibrated). Most Jackson glasswasher complaints resolve with 30-minute service + 10-minute chemistry calibration at $120 commercial diagnostic — chemistry side balanced alongside mechanical side on every bar call." },
  { q: "How often does a bar glass washer need cleaning?", a: "Daily glass washer maintenance discipline for commercial bar operations: (1) End of each bar shift — empty wash tank, wipe interior with damp cloth, inspect wash arm for debris. (2) Daily — verify detergent / rinse-aid / sanitizer dispenser levels topped, verify wash arms spin freely, verify drain functions properly. (3) Weekly — descale wash tank + wash arm jets with commercial descaler (LA hard water 8-12 grains/gallon makes this critical, otherwise mineral buildup degrades cleaning quality). (4) Monthly — pump seal visual inspection, motor amp draw check, chemistry calibration verification with test strips (sanitizer concentration 50-100 ppm chlorine target). (5) Annual PM — pump seal replacement preventively on year 4+ units ($260-$440), dispenser overhaul ($180-$320), spray arm bearing replacement if signs of wear ($180-$320). Annual PM service $300-$500 typical for bar glass washer fleet. Skip weekly descale and mineral buildup degrades cleaning quality within 4-6 weeks." },
  {
    q: "What's different about a glass washer vs an undercounter dishwasher?",
    a: "Glass washers run lower temp (130 to 140°F) to preserve etched and hand-blown glassware that high-temp dishwashers would etch. Cycles are faster (60 to 90 seconds vs 90 seconds to 4 minutes). Wash arms typically spin (rotational) rather than fixed-spray. Detergent and rinse aid concentrations are different. Different machine, different repair scope."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you service Hoshizaki HG-100, CMA Glass Mizer, and Champion CG series?",
    a: "Yes. These three platforms cover the LA bar glass washer market. Hoshizaki HG-100 (Hoshizaki commercial line), CMA Glass Mizer (Cleveland-based specialist), Champion CG-2 (Ali Group, sister brand to Scotsman ice and Beverage-Air refrigeration). We carry common dispenser solenoids, drain pumps, and water inlet valves on the van."
  },
  {
    q: "My glass washer's wash arms aren't spinning. What's wrong?",
    a: "Most common cause: jets clogged with bar residue (sugar syrup, citrus pulp, beer foam protein). Spinning relies on jet thrust, clogged jets means no rotation. Solution: deep clean of wash arm jets and inlet manifold. $200 to $340 service typical. If arm bearing has seized from sustained jet imbalance, replacement is $360 to $540."
  },
  {
    q: "Glass washer cycle is too short to actually clean glasses. Is that normal?",
    a: "Glass washers are designed for fast cycles (60 to 90 seconds) because bar service needs throughput. The trade-off is that pre-rinsing matters more, detergent feed rate must be calibrated, and rinse aid concentration controls spotting. If glassware is coming out dirty, the issue is typically detergent dispenser feed rate or jet clog, not cycle length."
  },
  {
    q: "How fast can you respond to a bar emergency?",
    a: "Same-day across Los Angeles, Orange, Ventura. Phones answered 24/7. Friday and Saturday evenings are our highest bar dispatch volume. No emergency surcharge, $120 anytime."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty?",
    a: "90 days SDAR labor warranty on every repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

