<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · What we service</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Bar glass washers, lower temp, faster cycles, etched-glass safe.</h2>
    <p>A commercial bar glass washer that produces hazy glassware, won't drain, or shows chemical dispenser issues in LA bar operations usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across West Hollywood craft-cocktail corridor, Arts District bar program operations, DTLA hotel bar service, Santa Monica beach-adjacent bars, and Beverly Hills luxury hotel bar programs running CMA Glass Mizer, Jackson Avenger LT / glasswasher, Champion CG-2, Lamb, Moyer Diebel, and Hoshizaki HG-100 commercial glass washer models. (1) Chemistry calibration issue — detergent dispenser, rinse-aid dispenser, or sanitizer pickup tube pinched / clogged / miscalibrated produces hazy glassware (most Jackson glasswasher complaints resolve with 30-minute service + 10-minute chemistry calibration). $180 to $320 dispenser rebuild + calibration. (2) Wash arm bearing wear year 5-8 — spray pattern degrades, glassware doesn't clean evenly. $180 to $320 bearing replacement. (3) Drain pump year 7-9 — pump motor failure means standing water, cycle won't complete. $280 to $440 drain pump replacement. $120 commercial diagnostic at Same Day Appliance Repair, waived with repair. Bar glass washers use low-temp chemical sanitizing rather than high-temp 180°F final rinse — different from full-size commercial dishwashers.</p>

    <p>Glass washers are bar-specific commercial dishwashers, designed differently from undercounter dishwashers. Lower wash temp (130 to 140°F vs 150 to 160°F on dishwashers) preserves etched, hand-blown, and gold-rim glassware that high-temp machines would etch or strip. Faster cycle times (60 to 90 seconds) keep up with bar service throughput. Spinning wash arms (rotational jet thrust) instead of fixed-spray manifolds.</p>

    <p>Three platforms dominate the LA bar segment: <strong>Hoshizaki HG-100</strong> (Hoshizaki commercial line, Japanese-engineered), <strong>CMA Glass Mizer</strong> (Cleveland-based commercial dishwasher specialist), <strong>Champion CG-2</strong> (Ali Group, sister brand to Scotsman ice and Beverage-Air). Plus Lamb LM and Moyer Diebel on legacy installs.</p>

    <p>BHGS #A49573. EPA 608 Universal certified #1346255700410. BBB Accredited. Phones answered 24/7. $120 commercial diagnostic, waived with repair, no emergency surcharge.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Typical glass washer failures</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Six failure modes account for most glass washer calls.</h2>
    <p>Across LA County commercial bar glass washer service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair dispatch — West Hollywood craft-cocktail corridor running Jackson Avenger LT + CMA Glass Mizer daily, Arts District bar program operations, DTLA hotel bar service (JW Marriott bar, Conrad lounge, InterContinental rooftop bar), Santa Monica beach-adjacent bars, Beverly Hills luxury hotel bar programs (Four Seasons, Peninsula), plus restaurant bar back-of-house operations — the failure distribution clusters predictably. About 30 percent chemistry calibration issue (detergent / rinse-aid / sanitizer dispenser, $180-$320 rebuild + calibration, single most common bar glass washer complaint). 20 percent wash arm bearing wear (year 5-8, $180-$320). 15 percent drain pump (year 7-9, $280-$440). 15 percent rinse pump motor (year 8-10, $380-$580). 10 percent door gasket compression (year 5-7, $180-$280). 10 percent fill solenoid + water level switch ($200-$340). Glass washers use low-temp chemical sanitizing — chemistry side balanced alongside mechanical side on every bar call.</p>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Wash arm jets clogged with bar residue.</strong> Sugar syrup, citrus pulp, beer foam protein, espresso oils, all clog small-diameter glass washer jets faster than dishwasher jets. Spinning relies on jet thrust, clogged jets means no rotation. Cleaning service $200 to $340.</li>
      <li><strong>Detergent and rinse aid dispensers.</strong> Glass washers run high-frequency dispense cycles. Solenoid coils corrode from chemical exposure faster than dishwasher solenoids. Replacement $260 to $400.</li>
      <li><strong>Drain pump (frequent cycling).</strong> Bar service produces 200+ cycles per shift on busy nights, drain pump impeller wear at year 4 to 6 typical. $300 to $480.</li>
      <li><strong>Door switch (frequent open/close at bar).</strong> Bartender opens and closes glass washer constantly during service. Switch wears at year 3 to 5. $200 to $340.</li>
      <li><strong>Water inlet valve.</strong> Hard Southern California water plus high-frequency cycling stresses inlet valve diaphragm. Failure at year 4 to 6. $280 to $440.</li>
      <li><strong>Wash arm bearing seizure.</strong> Sustained jet imbalance from clogged jets eventually seizes the arm bearing. Replacement $360 to $540 plus arm rebalancing.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

